  "narrative": "I use the controller's signed convention: for direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger, more negative dependency_composite; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker, less negative dependency_composite. The most consequential new result is H67, MSI-high in the broad screen-quality >=0.9 population. R108 is +0.779 [0.659, 0.899], a very large stronger-dependency contrast whose lower bound is far above the 0.15-unit threshold. This suggests that the MSI-high association is not confined to the strict TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact background in which it was first strongly supported and validated. Because H67 is a broad new context, arose after marker screening, and has substantial population-level impact, I request independent validation of H67 while currently accepting it as active. H137 tests the same marker after removing PTEN as a possible carrier: R109 is +0.741 [0.667, 0.816]. I accept and close it. H139 localizes the association to the adenocarcinoma subtype with TP53, KEAP1, and SMARCA4 excluded: R110 is +0.705 [0.613, 0.797], with lower bound well above threshold despite an exposed cell of 40. I accept and close it, noting small-cell caution but strong precision. Together, H67, H137, and H139 support MSI-high as a broad, dataset-specific stronger-dependency marker rather than a strict-background or subtype artifact.\n\nPTEN context tests are moderate but useful. H41, PTEN loss among TP53-intact high-quality lines, gives R112 +0.259 [0.165, 0.353], with the lower bound above threshold; I accept and close it. H40, PTEN among KEAP1-intact lines, gives R111 +0.212 [0.108, 0.316], and H44, PTEN among ARID1A-intact lines, gives R113 +0.210 [0.096, 0.324]. Both point estimates exceed threshold and are consistent with the accepted PTEN core, but their intervals include subthreshold effects, so I accept them as active rather than closed. H142, PTEN among low mutation-burden lines, gives R115 +0.258 [0.117, 0.400]; I accept it as active because it localizes PTEN toward lower TMB while the high-TMB PTEN context previously tested was null. The lower bounds are not all threshold-excluding, so I am not treating these as precise context-specific effects, but as plausible context-independent or context-localized extensions of the PTEN association.\n\nH141 tests a PTEN-by-TP53 interaction among KEAP1- and SMARCA4-intact lines. R114 is -0.141 [-0.488, 0.206]. The point estimate is opposite the claimed interaction direction, but the interval is very wide and includes both subthreshold negative effects and positive effects above threshold. The exposed interaction cell is small, so this is too imprecise to reject a meaningful interaction firmly, but the evidence does not support acceptance. I keep it unresolved and move it to deferred status because further same-dataset follow-up on this particular small-cell interaction is not high priority.\n\nThe SMARCA4 tests strongly confirm persistence of the dominant dataset-specific association. H144, SMARCA4 loss among high mutation-burden lines, has R116 +0.699 [0.515, 0.883]. H145, SMARCA4 loss among low-stemness lines, has R117 +0.863 [0.771, 0.955]. H147, SMARCA4 loss among PTEN-loss lines, has R119 +0.741 [0.528, 0.954]. All lower bounds are well above threshold, so I accept and close these as direct evidence that the SMARCA4 stronger-dependency contrast persists in tested genomic and phenotypic contexts. H146, SMARCA4 loss among MSI-high lines using a lowered screen-quality threshold of 0.85, has R118 +0.651 [0.431, 0.870]. The effect is strong and lower bound above threshold, but the reduced quality cutoff and smaller exposed cell make it less directly comparable to the main high-quality analyses; I accept it as active rather than closed. Overall, this batch supports a broader MSI-high finding, reinforces PTEN as a moderate stronger-dependency marker with some context localization, and further strengthens SMARCA4 as the dominant dataset-specific stronger-dependency marker.",
  "research_notes": "Round 9 appraise update. Signed convention: direction -1 positive means stronger/more negative dependency; direction +1 positive means weaker/less negative dependency. New MSI evidence substantially broadens the MSI-high finding. H67 broad screen>=0.9 MSI is accepted active and sent to validation: R108 +0.779 [0.659, 0.899]. H137 core-intact PTEN-intact MSI and H139 core-intact adenocarcinoma MSI are accepted closed, showing the association is not carried by PTEN co-occurrence and is not confined to non-adenocarcinoma lines. Together with validated H126 strict core-intact MSI, MSI-high is now among the strongest dataset-specific stronger-dependency markers, though the biological interpretation remains uncertain. PTEN context tests: H41 TP53-intact accepted closed (R112 +0.259 [0.165, 0.353]); H40 KEAP1-intact, H44 ARID1A-intact, and H142 low-TMB accepted active because point estimates are moderate but lower bounds include subthreshold values. H141 PTEN-by-TP53 interaction remains unresolved/deferred due wide interval and small exposed cells (R114 -0.141 [-0.488, 0.206]). SMARCA4 persistence tests are very robust: H144 high TMB accepted closed; H145 low stemness accepted closed; H147 PTEN-loss accepted closed; H146 MSI-high accepted active due lowered screen-quality threshold and smaller cells. Current dataset-specific supported core remains: SMARCA4 loss strongest and broad; MSI-high strong and broad after this batch plus strict validation; TP53 loss robust weaker-dependency; KEAP1 loss robust weaker-dependency; PTEN loss moderate stronger-dependency with validated main clean effects and context localization active; CDKN2A loss modest and less precisely localized. Negative/unsupported tested predictors remain PIK3CA, APC strict, NF1 strict, BRAF V600E, BRCA2, MTAP independent, ARID1A independent, STK11, EGFR, ERBB2, KRAS, RB1, research markers/signatures, and tested SMARCA4 adenocarcinoma interactions. Validation budget: one voluntary validation requested this iteration for H67. All claims remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal or externally generalizable.",
